e years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at -50% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $612M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Accruals are elevated at -10.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, interest coverage of 40\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Net dilution runs at 10.3% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and stock-based comp at 6267% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 11% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Very elevated short interest (20.2% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting against the business","sev":"red","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"ROIC sits in the bottom decile among Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 no moat advantage to speak of","sev":"red","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Consumer Cyclical peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Operating margins 30041% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (95% sell ratio, net $1186.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"F